00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:16.080
A lot of people, they run into
something that's too difficult

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:16.860
and they're discouraged.

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:21.720
Uh, the other thing of course, that's
very important is, uh, I haven't

00:16:21.780 --> 00:16:25.380
because I have an Arabic book and
I can't really read it yet, but the

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:27.210
audio has, the audio is so important.

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:33.210
Uh, most textbooks are narrated by people
who are very bored and if they're bored,

00:16:33.240 --> 00:16:34.700
then the person listening is bored.

00:16:35.520 --> 00:16:39.120
And so it's so important to
make the narration lively.

00:16:39.719 --> 00:16:43.020
Uh, and so that's again where
authentic material on YouTube is more

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:46.890
lively and therefore inherently more
interesting for people to listen to.

00:16:47.069 --> 00:16:49.709
And I think where there's a greater
resonance, then we learn better.

00:16:50.010 --> 00:16:52.459
And if it's boring, uh, we don't learn.

00:16:53.359 --> 00:16:53.569
Yeah.

00:16:53.569 --> 00:16:57.465
And that's, that is also one of the great
consequences I think, of the general

00:16:57.465 --> 00:17:02.595
